      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nRestrict the >=160 GiB batch-default tier to CUDA GPUs, preserving the existing non-CUDA tier. Refreshed against main `c5f8adc0`; related to #53961.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Retain 16384 server tokens for CUDA B200-class devices while using the existing 8192 tier for the mocked MI300X.\n- Update the existing platform fixture for main's GB10 capability detection instead of treating an unconfigured MagicMock result as true.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/engine/test_arg_utils.py -k large_memory_defaults_are_cuda_only -q` — **2 passed**.\n- The MI300X regression fails against unmodified main production code (`16384` instead of `8192`); the CUDA control passes.\n- Pre-commit on both changed files and `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` — **passed**.\n- An additional prefix-cache CLI test could not infer a device on this host. No real MI300X/B200 startup, memory or throughput evaluation ran here.\n\n## Details\n\nThe >=160 GiB branch is described as targeting B200/B300 but currently selects devices by capacity alone. The patch adds a CUDA predicate and retains main's separate GB10 detection and all other tiers.\n\n#53961 is closed after deployment/EP guidance, so this PR does not claim that issue remains open or that it resolves the full reported 1M-context startup failure. The narrower default-policy mismatch remains observable in the CPU regression; reviewer confirmation of the intended policy is requested.\n\nDuplicate check: re-read the issue and searched open PRs by issue number and CUDA batch defaults; no competing open fix for this predicate was found. Open since 2026-08-27. AI assistance was used, with signed-off, signed commits and Codex attribution. Human review and hardware validation remain required.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [ ] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [ ] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n**BEFORE SUBMITTING, PLEASE READ <https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/contributing>**\n",
