    {
      "body": "Hello @hmellor, when you have a chance, could you please review this PR? It addresses the CUDA-only batch-default behavior. Any feedback or guidance on the implementation and test coverage would be greatly appreciated. Thank you for your time!",
      "created_at": "2026-08-31T05:05:19Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/54043#issuecomment-5473976751",
      "id": 5473976751,
      "updated_at": "2026-08-31T05:05:19Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "ActiveSky"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Hi @hmellor, I merged main `c5f8adc0`, preserved its GB10 capability detection and adapted the existing platform fixture to that check. The refreshed description includes the current checklist, signed-off/AI attribution and validation limits.\n\nValidation: **2 focused tests passed** and pre-commit passed. On main the mocked MI300X still receives `16384` server tokens instead of `8192`; the CUDA control passes.\n\nThis PR has been open since **August 27**. #53961 is now closed after deployment/EP guidance, so I am not claiming a fresh reproduction of its full startup failure; the narrower capacity-versus-platform default-policy difference remains. Could you please confirm the intended policy and review the refreshed CUDA predicate? Hardware/serving validation has not been rerun here. Thank you.\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-15T06:19:03Z",
